; Works around reasonml/reason#2949: since Reason 3.16 (OCaml 5.2 parsetree),
; `(a, b) => e` parses as `fun a -> fun b -> e`, two one-argument closures,
; where OCaml syntax gives one two-argument function. Besides the allocation,
; a self tail call through such a function is no longer a loop under
; js_of_ocaml, so e.g. the evaluator's Trampoline.run overflows the stack.
; This rewriter fuses directly nested functions back together. Drop it once
; Reason parses multi-argument functions as one Pexp_function.

(library
 (name ppx_fuse_fun)
 (kind ppx_rewriter)
 (libraries ppxlib))
